# Copy to `deploy/.env` and fill in a real key before `docker compose up`.
# `docker-compose.yml`'s `jammi-server` service reads this via
# `${JAMMI_AUDIT_MASTER_KEY:?set it in .env}` — an ABSENT key fails compose
# up loudly rather than silently starting a server with no key at all. A
# PRESENT-but-malformed key still reaches the container; the server's own
# startup validation (crates/jammi-db/src/audit/key_store.rs) is what
# rejects that shape, reporting AuditError::MasterKey before it signs
# anything.
#
# Format: 64 hex characters (32 bytes). Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32

JAMMI_AUDIT_MASTER_KEY=
